id: pm-unwsns
title: "GH-825: restore SDK excess-property safety for extension definition metadata"
description: "Open index signatures on FlagDefinition and schema definition interfaces allow plausible misspellings to type-check, then abort runtime activation and drop later registrations."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:sdk",extensions,github-intake,type-safety
created_at: "2026-07-30T11:27:55.105Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T23:31:06.566Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-30T22:52:33.658Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-30T22:52:33.658Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Known-field interfaces enforce excess-property checking; any metadata escape hatch is explicitly namespaced; type tests reject name/type misspellings; activation remains atomic and suggests canonical fields
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make invalid extension metadata fail at author time while preserving explicit forward-compatible metadata
value: Package authors receive a compiler error before activation can partially register commands
impact: Closes a typed SDK/runtime contract gap across flags and schema definitions
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Misspelled flag and schema authoring properties fail TypeScript compilation before an extension can activate.
actual_result: "Known authoring metadata contracts are closed, explicit loose internal contracts are isolated, and type tests reject excess properties."
